                                            <msContents>
                                                <summary xml:lang="en">Pentateuch</summary>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-4-item-1">
                                                    <locus from="3v" to="4"/>
                                                    <title>Introduction</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <incipit>
                                                        <quote xml:lang="ar">المجد لله الذي اقرت العقول بوحدانيته</quote>
                                                    </incipit>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-4-item-2">
                                                    <locus from="4v" to="33"/>
                                                    <title>Genesis</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-4-item-3">
                                                    <locus from="33v" to="56v"/>
                                                    <title>Exodus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-4-item-4">
                                                    <locus from="57" to="72v"/>
                                                    <title>Leviticus</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-4-item-5">
                                                    <locus from="73" to="94"/>
                                                    <title>Numbers</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                </msItem>
                                                <msItem xml:id="bnf-arabe-4-item-6">
                                                    <locus from="94v" to="112v"/>
                                                    <title>Deuteronomy</title>
                                                    <textLang mainLang="ar"/>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">The version is that of Saʿīd ibn Yūsuf al-Fayyūmī.</note>
                                                </msItem>
                                            </msContents>
                                            <physDesc>
                                                <ab type="codicological-definition">
                                                    <objectType style="codex">Single manuscript</objectType>
                                                </ab>
                                                <objectDesc>
                                                    <supportDesc>
                                                        <support>
                                                            <material>Paper</material>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Oriental paper

BnF EAD physical description (srcphys_240da5f27c21047407d7fe): Gloses marginales en syriaque. — Note en syriaque sur les douze pierres précieuses du pectoral (f. 1) ; essais de plume (f. 1 v) ; table des livres de l&apos;Ancien Testament (f. 2 v). 23 lignes à la page. Surface écrite 300 × 200 mm. Cahiers numérotés en lettres arabes à 10 fol.Papier oriental.113 fol. (f. 2 laissé en blanc). Nombreux feuillets mutilés. Folioté en chiffres coptes.Écriture orientale (Égypte). — Titres rubriqués.350 × 260 mm.Reliure maroquin rouge. Armes et chiffres de Louis XV estampés à chaud.</note>
                                                        </support>
                                                        <extent>
                                                            <measure unit="folio">113 folios (f. 2 blank); many mutilated leaves; foliated in Coptic numerals</measure>
                                                            <dimensions>
                                                                <height unit="mm">350</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">260</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </extent>
                                                        <condition>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Because of its state of conservation, consultation is subject to authorization on motivated request.</note>
                                                        </condition>
                                                    </supportDesc>
                                                    <layoutDesc>
                                                        <summary>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">23 lines per page. Gatherings numbered in Arabic letters, 10 folios per gathering. Syriac marginal glosses; Syriac note on the twelve precious stones of the breastplate at f. 1; pen trials at f. 1v; table of Old Testament books at f. 2v.</note>
                                                        </summary>
                                                        <layout writtenLines="23" columns="1" xml:id="layout-1">
                                                            <dimensions type="written">
                                                                <height unit="mm">300</height>
                                                                <width unit="mm">200</width>
                                                            </dimensions>
                                                        </layout>
                                                    </layoutDesc>
                                                </objectDesc>
                                                <handDesc>
                                                    <summary xml:lang="en">Eastern Arabic hand, described as Egyptian.</summary>
                                                </handDesc>
                                                <scriptDesc>
                                                    <scriptNote script="arabic">
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Legacy hand scope: major.</note>
                                                    </scriptNote>
                                                </scriptDesc>
                                                <decoDesc>
                                                    <decoNote>
                                                        <note xml:lang="en">Rubricated titles.</note>
                                                    </decoNote>
                                                </decoDesc>
                                                <bindingDesc>
                                                    <binding>
                                                        <decoNote>
                                                            <note xml:lang="en">Red morocco binding with arms and ciphers of Louis XV stamped in gold.</note>
                                                        </decoNote>
                                                    </binding>
                                                </bindingDesc>
                                            </physDesc>
                                            <history>
                                                <summary>BnF EAD catalogue (srcphys_240da5f27c21047407d7fe): Pentateuque. Date described in the BnF catalogue: XIIIe siècle.</summary>
                                                <provenance>
                                                    <note xml:lang="en">Notices by Renaudot and J. Ascari (1735). From the Bibliothèque Mazarine. A note states that ownership passed from Ǧirǧis al-Qubruṣī to a priest whose name has been erased; reading mark of Buṭrus ibn Dīb al-Ḥalabī dated 1684 at f. 3; Syriac note on Israelite chronology at f. 113; pen trials at f. 113v.</note>
                                                </provenance>
                                                <origin>
                                                    <origDate calendar="#gregorian" notBefore="1201" notAfter="1300">13th century</origDate>
                                                    <p>Anonymous and undated copy.</p>
                                                </origin>
